WEBVTT

00:02:29.077 --> 00:02:32.976
(Laughter)

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.976
Let's take a look at it again.
Watch the coloration:

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.976
white on the right, brown on the left.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.711
He takes a step back,

00:02:41.735 --> 00:02:44.449
he's keeping off the other
males by splitting his body,

00:02:44.473 --> 00:02:46.176
and comes up on the other side --

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.264
Bingo!

00:02:47.288 --> 00:02:50.341
Now, I'm told that's not not just
a squid phenomenon with males,

00:02:50.365 --> 00:02:51.615
but I don't know.

00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:52.976
(Laughter)

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.898
Cuttlefish. I love cuttlefish.

00:02:54.922 --> 00:02:56.786
This is a Giant Australian Cuttlefish.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:59.282
And there he is,
his droopy little eyes up here.